    turnFlow: '1. **Ante**: All players post the ante. 2. **Market Setup**: Dealer turns up two cards and places them beside the deck. 3. **Buy Phase**: Starting left of dealer, each player buys one card from the market (face-up) or stock (top card, revealed on purchase). 4. **Refill**: Purchased market cards are replaced immediately from the stock. 5. **Bet Phase**: After each buy round, a standard betting round. 6. **Repetition**: Buy/bet sequence repeats 5 times until each player has 5 cards. 7. **Declaration**: Active players secret-declare High, Low, or Both using chips in hand. 8. **Showdown**: Cards revealed; pot split per declarations.',
    moveValidityConditions: {
      ante: 'Required for each player at start of hand before initial deal.',
      deal: 'Abyssinia uses buy rounds from market and stock; players build hands by purchasing cards, not by a traditional deal.',
      reveal_market: 'Dealer-only. Triggered automatically at market_setup phase.',
      buy_market: 'Must choose exactly one card from the 2-card market. Mandatory; cannot pass.',
      buy_stock: 'Must take top card blind. Card revealed face-up to all on purchase. Mandatory; cannot pass.',
      fold: 'Available during any betting round. Eliminates player from current hand.',
      check: 'Only legal when no bet has been opened in current round.',
      call: 'Only legal when a bet or raise exists. Must match exactly.',
      bet: 'Only legal when no bet opened yet. Sets current bet for others to call or raise.',
      raise: 'Only legal when bet or raise exists. Subject to fixed-limit raise caps.',
      declare: 'All active players declare simultaneously. 0=Low, 1=High, 2=Both. Pig Rule applies to Both.',
      reveal_hand: 'Triggered at showdown for all active players.',
      award_pot: 'Dealer-only. Split per declarations.',
      play_card: 'Abyssinia is poker, not trick-taking; players build 5-card hands by buying cards, with no play-to-table mechanic.',
